## 1. Material derived from Valve's Proton (lsteamclient)

The shim's cross-ABI facts are extracted from the PE-side sources of
ValveSoftware/Proton, pinned at tag `proton_11.0`, by
`src/shim/extract_vtables.py` and `src/shim/extract_structs.py`
(`src/shim/build.sh --regen-vtables` fetches them).

Derived artifacts committed here:

src/shim/vtables.json MSVC vtable slot order, i386 thiscall stack sizes,
and the declared parameter types of each method
src/shim/structs.json cross-ABI struct field layouts
src/shim/gen/\*.h C emitted from the above by gen_thunks.py and
gen_vtables.py: PE thunks, params structs, opcodes,
unix handlers, dispatch tables

Proton's root LICENSE delegates per directory. `LICENSE.proton` (BSD-3-Clause)
covers only top-level contents; `lsteamclient/LICENSE` is **Valve's Steamworks
SDK License Agreement**, and that is what governs the sources these artifacts
are read from. Note in particular its clause 1.1(a) (use in source form solely
to develop the Licensee Software), 1.3 (all rights not granted are reserved),
and 2.4 (no reverse engineering, and no developing software to replace the
SDK's functionality).

This project's posture, for the record: it reimplements no Steam logic. The
game links Valve's own unmodified `steam_api64.dll` redistributable, and what
ultimately answers is Valve's own macOS `steamclient.dylib`, hosted in process.
Calls travel _through_ Valve's API, not around it — the same posture as Proton,
which Valve itself ships. Whether that reading holds is Valve's call, not ours.
No legal opinion has been obtained. Anyone distributing builds of this software
should get one.

## 2. Valve binaries — used, never redistributed

`steamclient.dylib`, `gameoverlayrenderer.dylib` and the Steam client itself are
loaded from the user's own Steam installation at runtime. No Valve binary is
copied into, modified by, or shipped with this project, and Valve's files are
never modified in place.

## 3. CrossOver / CodeWeavers

CrossOver is a commercial product by CodeWeavers, required at runtime and not
distributed here. The shipping paths copy, re-sign and modify nothing inside
`CrossOver.app`; see docs/adr/0003-overlay-injection-at-process-creation.md.

## 4. Interface names and version strings

`src/shim/interface-versions.txt` and the interface/method names throughout are
facts about Valve's published Steamworks API surface, recorded to interoperate
with it.
